================================================================================
Bundled, linked, and vendored third-party components
================================================================================

rxd builds into a single binary and may embed or link the components below.
Each retains its own license and attribution; the files referenced here are the
authoritative notices. This summary does not replace them. Permissive licenses
(Apache-2.0, MIT, BSD) are compatible with rxd's Apache-2.0 license; their
notices are preserved on distribution.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Apache License 2.0 components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- rxd-dex: native APK/DEX backend migrated from rasc, incorporating code
  derived from jadx (Copyright 2015 Skylot) and the Android Open Source Project
  (Copyright 2007 The Android Open Source Project).
  See crates/rxd-dex/LICENSE.

- rxd-jvm: native JVM class-file frontend lifting bytecode into the radguard
  backend IR, with jadx-derived code. See crates/rxd-jvm/LICENSE and
  crates/rxd-jvm/NOTICE for the full upstream jadx attribution list. The jadx
  NOTICE enumerates jadx's own Java dependencies (including LGPL/EPL-licensed Logback and Eclipse icons);
  those Java components are NOT compiled or linked into the rxd binary and are
  reproduced only to preserve upstream attribution.

- third_party/radguard: vendored DEX decompiler and Java rendering backend
  (rxd's maintained fork of github.com/MG1937/radguard). Copyright 2026 The
  radguard Authors; an independent Rust implementation of the design and behavior
  of Androguard's DAD engine (Copyright 2015-2026 The Androguard Project).
  See third_party/radguard/LICENSE, NOTICE and FORK.md.

- third_party/kuna: optionally directly linked Kuna CLI (feature bundled-kuna).
  See third_party/kuna/LICENSE and third_party/kuna/NOTICE.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MIT License components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- third_party/pycdc: vendored Python bytecode decompiler engine
  (Copyright (c) 2026 ejfkdev). See third_party/pycdc/LICENSE.
  Provenance note: the relationship of this Rust source to the C++ pycdc project
  is documented as unknown in third_party/pycdc/NOTICE and is not inferred from
  the shared project name. That NOTICE is authoritative.

- ICSharpCode.Decompiler (ILSpy) 11.2.0.10050 and the .NET runtime: optionally
  bundled C# reconstruction engine (feature bundled-ilspy), downloaded from
  NuGet and built, not vendored (Copyright 2011-2026 AlphaSierraPapa, ILSpy
  Contributors; .NET runtime Copyright .NET Foundation and Contributors).
  See crates/rxd-dotnet/native/NOTICE.

- evmole 0.9.4: EVM bytecode analysis library (crates.io dependency).

- Oxc (oxc_ast, oxc_codegen and related crates) 0.153.0: Ark ECMAScript AST emission
  (crates.io dependency).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Dual-licensed components (MIT OR Apache-2.0)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- third_party/axmldecoder: AndroidManifest binary XML decoder, used under
  Apache-2.0. See third_party/axmldecoder/LICENSE.APACHE and LICENSE.MIT.

